{"action": "shrugs", "mood": "neutral", "internal_thought": "Lost a sheep, that's a worry", "language_hints": []}

Ah, now that was a bad business. I was there, helpin' to bring him home and tendin' to him till the breakin' set right. A cup of tea with a bit o' thyme might have eased the pain, but he was a stubborn one, refused to take it. I had to make sure he was comfortable till the swelling went down, sure. I was worried sick about him, mayhap more than he was himself.
---
{"action": "shakes head and sets down a wooden spoon in the nearby bowl", "mood": "concerned", "internal_thought": "The poor man's been limpin' ever since", "language_hints": []}

Ye'd best ask Seamus, the old fella who tends the farm up there. I've seen the lights meself, mayhap a fire or a lantern. 'Tis a fine sight, surely, but I'd not want to speculate. Mayhap 'twas just the fairies dancing, but 'tis better to leave such things to the imagination, don't ye think?
---
{"action": "shrugs, gestures to the hill", "mood": "cautious", "internal_thought": "Seamus might know, but best not to pry", "language_hints": [{"word": "sí", "pronunciation": "shee", "meaning": "fairy mound"}]}

Ah, 'tis a fine sight to see ye concerned for yer health. I've been checkin' the well water meself, and I think I might know what's causin' the taste. We've had a bit of a dry spell lately, and the soil's been prone to gettin' a wee bit alkaline. A tea of thyme might ease yer chest, but I'd recommend just lettin' it sit for a day or two to see if the taste clears up.
---
{"action": "nods and takes a step closer", "mood": "concerned", "internal_thought": "Possible high pH levels", "language_hints": []}

A wee lad on the way, is it? I'll need to come to ye the moment the pains start, or if the child doesn't come by the end of the week, whichever comes first. I'll be keepin' an ear out for any news, so I will. 'Twill be a fine sight when the wee one arrives.
---
{"action": "nods, makes a note on a piece of parchment", "mood": "calm", "internal_thought": "Seven months, if I recall, she said it was... and the moon's in the right phase, too", "language_hints": []}

Mayhap Father Cathal's words will bring some sense to the parishioners, but I think he forgets the simple things that have kept us alive for generations. A wee bit of respect for the sí, mayhap, wouldn't go amiss, but I suppose it's not for a priest to say such things.
